            "failureScenario": "save() passes the secret token straight to std::fs::write. The token is stored as plaintext at an arbitrary path. The file gets default permissions (subject to umask), with no encryption and no OS keychain. Any local user or process that can read the file, a backup, or a synced folder can recover the credential. The path is not validated, so a caller can place it in a shared or synced directory. The trailing unwrap() also panics on any I/O error, such as a missing directory, a full disk, or a permission failure. That crash can take down the process, and the panic message can expose the path. The clean variant stores the same token with keyring::Entry::set_password, so the planted version is a regression from the secure storage pattern. The supplied files contain no callers of this function.",
